class:: FFTFlux2
summary:: Explicit frame-to-frame spectral distance
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/FFTFlux

description::
Calculates the Euclidean distance between consecutive selected FFT spectra. Positive mode half-wave rectifies bin differences; normalized mode divides by the current frame norm. The first frame and silence return zero.

Previous-frame storage is allocated during construction from code::fftSize::, never when an FFT frame arrives. It is practically similar to link::Classes/FFTFlux:: and link::Classes/FFTFluxPos::, but unifies their behavior behind explicit positive, normalization, spectrum, and frequency options.

classmethods::

method:: kr

argument:: chain
An FFT chain matching code::fftSize::.

argument:: normalize
Nonzero divides distance by the current selected-spectrum norm.

argument:: positive
Nonzero ignores spectral decreases.

argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 compares magnitudes and 1 compares powers.

argument:: minFreq
Lowest included frequency in Hz.

argument:: maxFreq
Highest included frequency in Hz; 0 selects Nyquist.

argument:: fftSize
Literal FFT size from 256 through 8192.

returns::
Nonnegative spectral distance.

instancemethods::

examples::
Spectral flux measures frame-to-frame spectral distance. In this example, flux spikes trigger a dynamic granular scatter delay: sudden drum hits scatter into metallic micro-echoes while steady decaying tails remain focused. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: tracks the live flux detection curve.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic drum fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(2);
            var kick = SinOsc.ar(EnvGen.ar(Env([120, 45], [0.08], \exp), trig)) * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.3), trig);
            var snare = WhiteNoise.ar * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.15), Impulse.kr(2, 0.5));
            (kick + snare) * 0.5
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        var flux = FFTFlux2.kr(chain, positive: 1, fftSize: 1024);
        var scatterGate = (flux * 6.0).clip(0.0, 1.0).lag(0.02);
        var scatter = CombC.ar(source, 0.1, [0.03, 0.045], 0.3) * scatterGate;
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + (scatter.sum * 0.25);

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, flux) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Spectral Flux", ~mir2Bus, 0.0, 15.0);
});
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

